    " \"cells\": [\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Science Data Kit: Interactive Tutorial\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"This notebook provides an interactive introduction to the Science Data Kit (SDK) for scientific data analysis. You can run the code cells to see how the SDK works and experiment with its features.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Prerequisites\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Before running this notebook, make sure you have:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"1. Installed the Science Data Kit (`pip install science-data-kit`)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"2. Set up a Neo4j database (either locally or using Docker)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"3. Downloaded the example datasets from the SDK repository\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## 1. Setting Up\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"First, let's import the necessary modules and check that everything is installed correctly.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Import core SDK modules\\n\",\n",
    "    \"from science_data_kit.core.db.db_manager import DBManager\\n\",\n",
    "    \"from science_data_kit.core.session.session import create_session\\n\",\n",
    "    \"from science_data_kit.core.utils.model_training import train_model\\n\",\n",
    "    \"from science_data_kit.core.analysis.sklearn_integration import prepare_data, evaluate_model\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Import other useful libraries\\n\",\n",
    "    \"import pandas as pd\\n\",\n",
    "    \"import numpy as np\\n\",\n",
    "    \"import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\\n\",\n",
    "    \"import seaborn as sns\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Set up plotting\\n\",\n",
    "    \"%matplotlib inline\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.style.use('ggplot')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"sns.set(style=\\\"whitegrid\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Print SDK version\\n\",\n",
    "    \"import science_data_kit\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Science Data Kit version: {science_data_kit.__version__}\\\")\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"### 1.1 Connecting to Neo4j\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Let's connect to our Neo4j database. If you're using the Docker setup, the default credentials should work.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Create a database manager\\n\",\n",
    "    \"db_manager = DBManager()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Check if connected\\n\",\n",
    "    \"if db_manager.is_connected():\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(\\\"Connected to Neo4j database\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\n\",\n",
    "    \"    # Get database info\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    success, result = db_manager.query(\\\"CALL dbms.components() YIELD name, versions, edition RETURN name, versions, edition\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    if success:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        print(f\\\"Database: {result[0]['name']} {result[0]['edition']} {result[0]['versions'][0]}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"else:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(\\\"Not connected to Neo4j database. Please check your connection settings.\\\")\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"### 1.2 Creating a Session\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Now, let's create a session to track our analysis. Sessions in the SDK help you organize your work and make it reproducible.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Create a session\\n\",\n",
    "    \"session = create_session(\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    name=\\\"Interactive Tutorial\\\",\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    description=\\\"Analysis of environmental data using the Science Data Kit\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Print session information\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Session ID: {session.session_id}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Session name: {session.config.name}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Session description: {session.config.description}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Session created: {session.config.created}\\\")\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## 2. Loading and Exploring Data\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"For this tutorial, we'll use a sample environmental dataset. Let's load it and explore its structure.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Load the environmental data\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Replace with the path to your dataset\\n\",\n",
    "    \"data_path = \\\"../../../data/samples/environmental_data.csv\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"try:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    env_data = pd.read_csv(data_path)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(f\\\"Loaded dataset with {len(env_data)} rows and {len(env_data.columns)} columns\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"except FileNotFoundError:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(f\\\"File not found: {data_path}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(\\\"Creating a synthetic dataset for demonstration purposes...\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\n\",\n",
    "    \"    # Create a synthetic dataset\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    np.random.seed(42)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    dates = pd.date_range(start='2023-01-01', periods=365, freq='D')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\n\",\n",
    "    \"    env_data = pd.DataFrame({\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'timestamp': dates,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'temperature': np.random.normal(15, 5, 365) + 10 * np.sin(np.linspace(0, 2*np.pi, 365)),  # Seasonal pattern\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'humidity': np.random.normal(60, 10, 365),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'air_quality': np.random.normal(50, 15, 365),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'wind_speed': np.random.exponential(4, 365),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'precipitation': np.random.exponential(2, 365) * (np.random.random(365) > 0.7)  # Many zeros\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    })\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\n\",\n",
    "    \"    # Add some anomalies\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    env_data.loc[50:55, 'temperature'] += 15  # Heat wave\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    env_data.loc[200:202, 'air_quality'] += 100  # Pollution event\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(f\\\"Created synthetic dataset with {len(env_data)} rows and {len(env_data.columns)} columns\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Set timestamp as index if it exists\\n\",\n",
    "    \"if 'timestamp' in env_data.columns:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    env_data['timestamp'] = pd.to_datetime(env_data['timestamp'])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    env_data.set_index('timestamp', inplace=True)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Display the first few rows\\n\",\n",
    "    \"env_data.head()\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"### 2.1 Data Summary\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Let's get a summary of the data to understand its characteristics.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Display summary statistics\\n\",\n",
    "    \"env_data.describe()\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Check for missing values\\n\",\n",
    "    \"missing_values = env_data.isnull().sum()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(\\\"Missing values per column:\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(missing_values)\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"### 2.2 Data Visualization\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Let's visualize the data to better understand its patterns and relationships.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Time series plot of temperature\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.figure(figsize=(12, 6))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"env_data['temperature'].plot()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.title('Temperature Over Time')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.ylabel('Temperature (°C)')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.grid(True)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.show()\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Correlation matrix\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.figure(figsize=(10, 8))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"correlation_matrix = env_data.corr()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"sns.heatmap(correlation_matrix, annot=True, cmap='coolwarm', vmin=-1, vmax=1)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.title('Correlation Matrix')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.tight_layout()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.show()\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Pairplot for key variables\\n\",\n",
    "    \"sns.pairplot(env_data[['temperature', 'humidity', 'air_quality']])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.suptitle('Pairplot of Key Environmental Variables', y=1.02)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.show()\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## 3. Data Preprocessing\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Now, let's preprocess the data to prepare it for analysis and modeling.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Handle missing values using forward fill (common for time series)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"env_data_clean = env_data.ffill()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Remove outliers using IQR method\\n\",\n",
    "    \"def remove_outliers(df, columns=None):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    if columns is None:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        columns = df.select_dtypes(include=[np.number]).columns\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\n\",\n",
    "    \"    df_clean = df.copy()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\n\",\n",
    "    \"    for column in columns:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        Q1 = df[column].quantile(0.25)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        Q3 = df[column].quantile(0.75)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        IQR = Q3 - Q1\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        \\n\",\n",
    "    \"        lower_bound = Q1 - 1.5 * IQR\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        upper_bound = Q3 + 1.5 * IQR\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        \\n\",\n",
    "    \"        df_clean[column] = df[column].clip(lower_bound, upper_bound)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\n\",\n",
    "    \"    return df_clean\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"env_data_clean = remove_outliers(env_data_clean)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Compare original and cleaned data\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.figure(figsize=(12, 6))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.plot(env_data.index, env_data['temperature'], label='Original', alpha=0.7)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.plot(env_data_clean.index, env_data_clean['temperature'], label='Cleaned', alpha=0.7)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.title('Temperature: Original vs. Cleaned')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.ylabel('Temperature (°C)')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.legend()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.grid(True)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.show()\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"### 3.1 Feature Engineering\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Let's create some additional features that might be useful for analysis and modeling.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Add date-based features\\n\",\n",
    "    \"env_data_features = env_data_clean.copy()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"env_data_features['month'] = env_data_features.index.month\\n\",\n",
    "    \"env_data_features['day_of_week'] = env_data_features.index.dayofweek\\n\",\n",
    "    \"env_data_features['is_weekend'] = env_data_features['day_of_week'].isin([5, 6]).astype(int)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Add rolling statistics\\n\",\n",
    "    \"env_data_features['temp_rolling_mean_7d'] = env_data_features['temperature'].rolling(window=7).mean()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"env_data_features['temp_rolling_std_7d'] = env_data_features['temperature'].rolling(window=7).std()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Add lag features\\n\",\n",
    "    \"env_data_features['temp_lag_1d'] = env_data_features['temperature'].shift(1)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"env_data_features['temp_lag_7d'] = env_data_features['temperature'].shift(7)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Drop rows with NaN values (from rolling windows and lags)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"env_data_features = env_data_features.dropna()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Display the first few rows with new features\\n\",\n",
    "    \"env_data_features.head()\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## 4. Anomaly Detection\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Let's use the SDK to detect anomalies in our environmental data.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Simple anomaly detection using Z-scores\\n\",\n",
    "    \"def detect_anomalies(df, columns=None, threshold=3.0):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    if columns is None:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        columns = df.select_dtypes(include=[np.number]).columns\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\n\",\n",
    "    \"    anomalies = {}\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    z_scores = {}\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\n\",\n",
    "    \"    for column in columns:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        # Calculate Z-scores\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        mean = df[column].mean()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        std = df[column].std()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        z_scores[column] = (df[column] - mean) / std\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        \\n\",\n",
    "    \"        # Identify anomalies (|Z| > threshold)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        anomalies[column] = df[abs(z_scores[column]) > threshold]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\n\",\n",
    "    \"    return anomalies, z_scores\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Detect anomalies in the original data\\n\",\n",
    "    \"anomalies, z_scores = detect_anomalies(env_data, columns=['temperature', 'air_quality'])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Print anomaly counts\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(\\\"Anomaly counts:\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"for column, anomaly_df in anomalies.items():\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(f\\\"{column}: {len(anomaly_df)} anomalies\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Plot temperature with anomalies highlighted\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.figure(figsize=(12, 6))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.plot(env_data.index, env_data['temperature'], label='Temperature', alpha=0.7)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"if len(anomalies['temperature']) > 0:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    plt.scatter(\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        anomalies['temperature'].index,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        anomalies['temperature']['temperature'],\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        color='red',\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        label='Anomalies',\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        zorder=5\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    )\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.title('Temperature Time Series with Anomalies')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.ylabel('Temperature (°C)')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.legend()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.grid(True)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.show()\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## 5. Predictive Modeling\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Now, let's use the SDK's machine learning capabilities to build a predictive model for temperature.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Prepare data for modeling\\n\",\n",
    "    \"target_column = 'temperature'\\n\",\n",
    "    \"feature_columns = ['month', 'day_of_week', 'is_weekend', 'humidity', 'air_quality', \\n\",\n",
    "    \"                   'temp_rolling_mean_7d', 'temp_rolling_std_7d', 'temp_lag_1d', 'temp_lag_7d']\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Create a DataFrame with features and target\\n\",\n",
    "    \"model_data = env_data_features[feature_columns + [target_column]].copy()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Split the data into training and testing sets\\n\",\n",
    "    \"X_train, X_test, y_train, y_test = prepare_data(\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    model_data, \\n\",\n",
    "    \"    target_column=target_column, \\n\",\n",
    "    \"    test_size=0.3, \\n\",\n",
    "    \"    random_state=42\\n\",\n",
    "    \")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Training set size: {len(X_train)}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Testing set size: {len(X_test)}\\\")\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Train a gradient boosting model\\n\",\n",
    "    \"from sklearn.ensemble import GradientBoostingRegressor\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"model, results = train_model(\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    GradientBoostingRegressor(n_estimators=100, random_state=42),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    X_train,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    y_train,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    model_type='sklearn',\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    cross_validate=True,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    cv=5,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    scoring=['r2', 'neg_mean_squared_error', 'neg_mean_absolute_error']\\n\",\n",
    "    \")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Print cross-validation results\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(\\\"Cross-validation results:\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"for metric, values in results.items():\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    if isinstance(values, list):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        if 'neg_' in metric:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            # Convert negative metrics to positive\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            values = [-v for v in values]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            metric = metric.replace('neg_', '')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        print(f\\\"{metric}: {sum(values)/len(values):.4f}\\\")\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Evaluate the model on the test set\\n\",\n",
    "    \"test_metrics = evaluate_model(model, X_test, y_test, is_classifier=False)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Print test metrics\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(\\\"Test metrics:\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"for metric, value in test_metrics.items():\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(f\\\"{metric}: {value:.4f}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Make predictions\\n\",\n",
    "    \"y_pred = model.predict(X_test)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Plot actual vs predicted values\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.figure(figsize=(10, 6))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.scatter(y_test, y_pred, alpha=0.5)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.plot([y_test.min(), y_test.max()], [y_test.min(), y_test.max()], 'k--')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.xlabel('Actual Temperature')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.ylabel('Predicted Temperature')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.title('Actual vs Predicted Temperature')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.grid(True)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.show()\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Feature importance\\n\",\n",
    "    \"feature_importance = pd.DataFrame({\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    'feature': feature_columns,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    'importance': model.feature_importances_\\n\",\n",
    "    \"}).sort_values('importance', ascending=False)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Plot feature importance\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.figure(figsize=(10, 6))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"sns.barplot(x='importance', y='feature', data=feature_importance)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.title('Feature Importance for Temperature Prediction')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.tight_layout()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.show()\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## 6. Storing Results in Neo4j\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Now, let's store our analysis results in Neo4j for future reference and sharing.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Save the model\\n\",\n",
    "    \"import os\\n\",\n",
    "    \"from science_data_kit.core.analysis.sklearn_integration import save_model\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Create a directory for models if it doesn't exist\\n\",\n",
    "    \"os.makedirs(\\\"models\\\", exist_ok=True)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Save the model\\n\",\n",
    "    \"model_path = os.path.join(\\\"models\\\", \\\"temperature_prediction_model.pkl\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"success, message = save_model(model, model_path)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"if success:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(f\\\"Model saved successfully: {message}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"else:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(f\\\"Failed to save model: {message}\\\")\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Store results in Neo4j\\n\",\n",
    "    \"with db_manager.transaction() as tx:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    # Create a study node\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    study_query = \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    CREATE (s:EnvironmentalStudy {id: $study_id, name: $study_name, description: $study_description})\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    RETURN s\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    study_params = {\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'study_id': f\\\"ENV_STUDY_{session.session_id}\\\",\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'study_name': session.config.name,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'study_description': session.config.description\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    }\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    tx.run(study_query, study_params)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\n\",\n",
    "    \"    # Create a model node\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    model_query = \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    MATCH (s:EnvironmentalStudy {id: $study_id})\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    CREATE (m:Model {\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        type: $model_type,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        target: $target,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        r2_score: $r2_score,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        rmse: $rmse,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        mae: $mae,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        model_path: $model_path\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    })\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    CREATE (s)-[r:HAS_MODEL]->(m)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    RETURN m\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    model_params = {\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'study_id': f\\\"ENV_STUDY_{session.session_id}\\\",\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'model_type': 'GradientBoostingRegressor',\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'target': 'temperature',\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'r2_score': float(test_metrics.get('r2', 0)),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'rmse': float(test_metrics.get('rmse', 0)),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'mae': float(test_metrics.get('mae', 0)),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'model_path': model_path\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    }\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    tx.run(model_query, model_params)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\n\",\n",
    "    \"    # Store top features\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    top_features = feature_importance.head(5)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    for _, feature in top_features.iterrows():\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        feature_query = \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        MATCH (m:Model)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        WHERE m.model_path = $model_path\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        CREATE (f:Feature {name: $feature_name, importance: $importance})\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        CREATE (m)-[r:HAS_IMPORTANT_FEATURE]->(f)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        RETURN f\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        feature_params = {\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            'model_path': model_path,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            'feature_name': feature['feature'],\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            'importance': float(feature['importance'])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        }\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        tx.run(feature_query, feature_params)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\n\",\n",
    "    \"    # Store anomalies\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    for column, anomaly_df in anomalies.items():\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        if len(anomaly_df) > 0:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            anomaly_query = \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            MATCH (s:EnvironmentalStudy {id: $study_id})\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            CREATE (a:AnomalyGroup {\\n\",\n",
    "    \"                parameter: $parameter,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"                count: $count,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"                detection_method: $method\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            })\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            CREATE (s)-[r:HAS_ANOMALIES]->(a)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            RETURN a\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            anomaly_params = {\\n\",\n",
    "    \"                'study_id': f\\\"ENV_STUDY_{session.session_id}\\\",\\n\",\n",
    "    \"                'parameter': column,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"                'count': len(anomaly_df),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"                'method': 'Z-score'\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            }\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            tx.run(anomaly_query, anomaly_params)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(\\\"Results stored in Neo4j database\\\")\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Save analysis results to the session\\n\",\n",
    "    \"session.add_metadata({\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    'data_timespan': f\\\"{env_data.index.min()} to {env_data.index.max()}\\\",\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    'num_anomalies': sum(len(anomalies[col]) for col in anomalies),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    'model_r2': test_metrics.get('r2', None),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    'model_rmse': test_metrics.get('rmse', None),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    'model_path': model_path,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    'top_features': top_features['feature'].tolist()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"})\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Save the session\\n\",\n",
    "    \"session.save()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Session saved with ID: {session.session_id}\\\")\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## 7. Querying Neo4j\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Let's query Neo4j to retrieve our stored results.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Query for studies\\n\",\n",
    "    \"success, studies = db_manager.query(\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"MATCH (s:EnvironmentalStudy)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"RETURN s.id as id, s.name as name, s.description as description\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\\"\\\"\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"if success and studies:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(\\\"Environmental Studies in Neo4j:\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    for study in studies:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        print(f\\\"ID: {study['id']}, Name: {study['name']}, Description: {study['description']}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"else:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(\\\"No environmental studies found in Neo4j\\\")\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Query for models and their features\\n\",\n",
    "    \"success, models = db_manager.query(\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"MATCH (s:EnvironmentalStudy)-[:HAS_MODEL]->(m:Model)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"RETURN s.name as study_name, m.type as model_type, m.target as target, \\n\",\n",
    "    \"       m.r2_score as r2_score, m.rmse as rmse, m.mae as mae\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\\"\\\"\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"if success and models:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(\\\"Models in Neo4j:\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    for model in models:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        print(f\\\"Study: {model['study_name']}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        print(f\\\"Model Type: {model['model_type']}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        print(f\\\"Target: {model['target']}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        print(f\\\"R² Score: {model['r2_score']:.4f}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        print(f\\\"RMSE: {model['rmse']:.4f}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        print(f\\\"MAE: {model['mae']:.4f}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        print(\\\"---\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"else:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(\\\"No models found in Neo4j\\\")\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Query for features\\n\",\n",
    "    \"success, features = db_manager.query(\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"MATCH (m:Model)-[:HAS_IMPORTANT_FEATURE]->(f:Feature)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"RETURN m.target as target, f.name as feature, f.importance as importance\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ORDER BY importance DESC\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\\"\\\"\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"if success and features:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(\\\"Important Features in Neo4j:\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    for feature in features:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        print(f\\\"Target: {feature['target']}, Feature: {feature['feature']}, Importance: {feature['importance']:.4f}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"else:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(\\\"No features found in Neo4j\\\")\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## 8. Loading a Session\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Let's see how to load a session to continue our analysis later.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"from science_data_kit.core.session.session import load_session, list_sessions\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# List available sessions\\n\",\n",
    "    \"sessions = list_sessions()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Available sessions: {len(sessions)}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"for session_info in sessions:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(f\\\"  {session_info['name']} - {session_info['description']}\\\")\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Load our session\\n\",\n",
    "    \"loaded_session = load_session(session.session_file)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Print session information\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Loaded session ID: {loaded_session.session_id}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Loaded session name: {loaded_session.config.name}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Loaded session created: {loaded_session.config.created}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Loaded session metadata:\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"for key, value in loaded_session.metadata.items():\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(f\\\"  {key}: {value}\\\")\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## 9. Loading a Model\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Finally, let's see how to load a saved model for making predictions.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"from science_data_kit.core.analysis.sklearn_integration import load_model\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Load the model\\n\",\n",
    "    \"success, loaded_model = load_model(model_path)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"if success:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(\\\"Model loaded successfully\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\n\",\n",
    "    \"    # Make predictions with the loaded model\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    sample_data = X_test[:5]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    predictions = loaded_model.predict(sample_data)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\n\",\n",
    "    \"    # Compare with actual values\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    comparison = pd.DataFrame({\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'Actual': y_test[:5].values,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'Predicted': predictions,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'Difference': y_test[:5].values - predictions\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    })\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(\\\"\\\\nPredictions from loaded model:\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(comparison)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"else:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(f\\\"Failed to load model: {loaded_model}\\\")\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## Conclusion\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
